 @Aphriot  Right, but you tried to correct the original video. The original video said it increased input lag and THEY were talking about over native. Then YOU said “Actually it doesn’t increase input lag over DLSS 3.5” as if thats what they were even talking about.
I never said you were talking about native, work on your literacy.

Edit: I capitalised some words to help you out. 😘

 @Firestarter9  Damn here I am talking about not being confusing and then I go and be confusing. I did say DLSS increases input lag, but I really meant the Frame Gen aspect not the Upscaling part. Idk why they included FG as part of DLSS when it could be separate. 
The upscaling aspect of DLSS can give you better latency because you’re rending at a lower resolution, but the added latency from FG destroys any gains usually. The only way you’d have better latency running FG is if your DLSS is upscaling from a resolution low enough that you can’t even compare the image quality to native. I could be wrong but I havent seen one example where someone has gotten better latency using Frame Gen.

I edited my comment thanks 😂
